# FPGA Edge AI Image Enhancement
> A hardware-accelerated image enhancement pipeline using Residual CNNs, INT8 quantization, and Xilinx Vitis AI for real-time FPGA inference.
---
## Overview
Most image enhancement systems are designed and evaluated entirely on CPUs or GPUs:
```python
model(image)

This project takes a deployment-first approach — building an FPGA-oriented deep learning pipeline optimized for low-latency edge inference using INT8 quantization and Xilinx DPU acceleration.

The system combines Residual CNN architectures with Quantization-Aware Training (QAT), Vitis AI compilation, and FPGA deployment to achieve efficient real-time image enhancement for embedded AI systems.

⸻

Features

Component	Implementation
Deep Learning Model	Residual CNN architecture
Optimization	INT8 Quantization-Aware Training
FPGA Deployment	Xilinx Vitis AI workflow
Hardware Acceleration	DPU-based inference
Enhancement Tasks	Low-light enhancement, denoising, blur restoration
Evaluation Metrics	PSNR and SSIM analysis
Runtime Environment	Docker-based deployment
Inference Target	Edge AI / FPGA systems

No TensorRT. No GPU dependency during deployment. Optimized specifically for FPGA inference pipelines.

⸻

Project Structure

FPGA-Image-Enhancement/
│
├── models/                 # Trained models and compiled xmodels
├── testing_code/           # Inference and evaluation scripts
├── testing_images/         # Sample input images
├── output/                 # Enhanced outputs
├── results/                # Benchmark and evaluation results
├── docs/                   # Documentation and reports
│
├── Dockerfile
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md

⸻

Quick Start

Option 1 — Docker (Recommended)

Docker provides a reproducible environment for inference and deployment.

# Build Docker image
docker build -t fpga-enhancement .
# Run container
docker run -it fpga-enhancement

⸻

Option 2 — Local Installation

Requirements

* Python 3.10+
* PyTorch
* Vitis AI Runtime
* Xilinx FPGA platform

⸻

Step 1 — Clone Repository

git clone https://github.com/your-username/FPGA-Image-Enhancement.git
cd FPGA-Image-Enhancement

⸻

Step 2 — Install Dependencies

pip install -r requirements.txt

⸻

Step 3 — Run Inference

python testing_code/test.py

⸻

System Pipeline

Input Image
    │
    ▼
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ Residual CNN Training    │  Learn enhancement mappings using residual blocks
└────────────┬─────────────┘
             │
             ▼
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ Quantization-Aware Train │  Simulate INT8 arithmetic during training
└────────────┬─────────────┘
             │
             ▼
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ INT8 Optimization        │  Reduce precision for FPGA efficiency
└────────────┬─────────────┘
             │
             ▼
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ Vitis AI Compilation     │  Compile model for Xilinx DPU architecture
└────────────┬─────────────┘
             │
             ▼
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ XModel Generation        │  Generate deployable FPGA model
└────────────┬─────────────┘
             │
             ▼
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ FPGA DPU Inference       │  Accelerated hardware execution
└────────────┬─────────────┘
             │
             ▼
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ Enhanced Output Image    │  Denoised and restored image output
└──────────────────────────┘

⸻

Technical Reference

Residual CNN Architecture

* Uses residual learning to preserve low-frequency image information
* Helps stabilize deeper convolutional training
* Improves enhancement quality without excessive parameter growth

Quantization-Aware Training (QAT)

* Simulates INT8 precision during training
* Reduces post-quantization accuracy degradation
* Produces FPGA-friendly inference models

INT8 Optimization

* Converts floating-point operations into fixed-point arithmetic
* Reduces memory bandwidth and compute overhead
* Enables efficient DPU execution

Vitis AI Deployment

* Model compiled using Xilinx Vitis AI toolchain
* Generates .xmodel deployment artifacts
* Targets FPGA-based DPU accelerators

DPU Hardware Acceleration

* Offloads CNN inference from CPU to FPGA fabric
* Enables real-time edge inference
* Improves throughput and energy efficiency

Evaluation Metrics

* PSNR (Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio) for reconstruction quality
* SSIM (Structural Similarity Index) for perceptual similarity

⸻

Performance

Metric	CPU Execution	FPGA DPU
Precision	FP32	INT8
Inference Speed	0.85 – 1.3 FPS	8.37 FPS
Deployment Target	CPU	FPGA
Relative Speed	1×	8–10× Faster

The FPGA implementation significantly improves inference throughput while maintaining acceptable enhancement quality under INT8 quantization.

⸻

FPGA Deployment Workflow

The deployment pipeline includes:

PyTorch Model
      ↓
Quantization
      ↓
Vitis AI Compiler
      ↓
.xmodel Generation
      ↓
DPU Runtime Deployment
      ↓
FPGA Inference

Compiled deployment artifact:

models/model_b8_c128_int.xmodel

